#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Round D (verify + deepen, slower effort) -> Round E (critique of the deepened options) -> Round F (memo v2).
set -u
R=/Users/neo/repos/polyformer
D=$R/research/meta/chew
CODEX=/Applications/ChatGPT.app/Contents/Resources/codex-cli/bin/codex
AGY=/Applications/Gemini.app/Contents/Helpers/agy
COMMON="Read $D/CHEW_CONTEXT.md, $D/C_memo.md (the first-pass memo) and $R/research/meta/survive/AUDIT.md (what survives of our higher-order and Nerode results). You may read any file under $R and /Users/neo/repos/sketchpad but change nothing. Search the live web thoroughly and slowly; this is the deep pass, depth beats speed. Cite every paper with authors, year, venue/arXiv id and one line on what it did; open each paper you rely on; never invent citations (write 'unverified'). Your final message IS your report: markdown, no preamble."
cx() { "$CODEX" --search exec -s read-only --skip-git-repo-check -C "$R" -c model_reasoning_effort="xhigh" -o "$D/$1.md" "$2" > "$D/logs/$1.log" 2>&1 < /dev/null; }
ag() { (cd "$R" && "$AGY" -p "$3" --model "$2" --dangerously-skip-permissions --print-timeout 0 > "$D/$1.md" 2> "$D/logs/$1.log" < /dev/null); }
echo "D start $(date)" >> "$D/logs/progress2.txt"
cx D1_citations "$COMMON
Your role: CITATION AUDITOR. For every paper cited in $D/C_memo.md, $D/B1_gate.md and $D/A1_nature_anatomy.md, check on the live web that it exists, that authors/year/venue/id are right, and that it says what our reports claim. Output one table: citation | exists? | details correct? | claim supported? | note. Flag every fabricated or mis-described paper loudly. At most 1,500 words." &
cx D2_arity "$COMMON
Your role: THE ARITY OF THOUGHT. Our surviving theory (AUDIT.md sections 2, 3, 5): attention whose logits are sums of pairwise terms is blind to k-way relations (order-k blindness, coupling barrier); k-way terms (cubic, Newton power sums) fix it. Cognitive science has relational complexity theory (Halford, Wilson & Phillips 1998 BBS; later work by Halford, Phillips, Andrews, Doumas, Holyoak, Webb): human working memory is limited by the ARITY of relations processed in parallel (about 4). Investigate deeply: is there a direction where a formal result about attention arity explains or predicts human relational capacity limits (or LLM failures on relational tasks) better than existing accounts, and which could be tested WITHOUT new human data (existing human datasets: e.g. relational reasoning, Raven-like, analogy, sentence processing) or with a cheap online study? Map prior art thoroughly (incl. Webb, Holyoak & Lu 2023 Nature Human Behaviour; LISA/DORA; relational bottleneck work by Webb, Frankland, Cohen; tensor-product binding; capacity limits in transformers). Propose the strongest version with a draft title, decisive test, kill, cost. At most 1,600 words." &
ag D3_grammar claude-opus-5-5-high "$COMMON
Your role: THE DISCOVERY MACHINE FOR GRAMMAR (direction 2 of the memo, Neo's favourite theme: 'young Chomsky with LLMs'). Design it seriously: how would an LLM-informant procedure (Harris distributional analysis / Clark learners / meaning-matched minimal pairs, avoiding the Hu et al. 2026 TACL confound) actually surface a NEW, true grammatical generalisation? Which languages or constructions are under-described yet well covered by open multilingual models (check Qwen3.5 language coverage)? Which public human-judgment datasets allow validation without running new participants (e.g. Sprouse et al. 2013, BLiMP, CLiMP, SyntaxGym, multilingual acceptability sets, Grambank/WALS for typology)? What would a linguist collaborator need to see? Give a concrete 2-week pilot with numbers and a kill. Verify prior art live (incl. Yu et al. 2026 arXiv:2604.07189 if it exists, Goertzel 2020, LLM-for-linguistics-discovery papers). At most 1,600 words." &
cx D4_nohumans "$COMMON
Your role: NO-NEW-HUMANS OPTIONS. Neo is one researcher; new human-subject studies need ethics approval, recruitment and time. Find directions with Nature/Nature Human Behaviour/PNAS-level potential that need NO new human data: they use existing public human datasets (behavioural, acceptability, reading times, eye tracking, fMRI/ECoG such as Narratives, Pereira, Natural Stories), typological databases (WALS, Grambank), corpora, or mathematics/formal proof, combined with LLM fine-tuning, model dissection and our theory (Nerode classes, higher-order attention, certification). For each candidate: what old question it answers, the decisive analysis, prior art (verified live), and why it could survive review. Give 5 candidates ranked. At most 1,500 words." &
wait
echo "E start $(date)" >> "$D/logs/progress2.txt"
ag E1_referee claude-opus-5-5-high "$COMMON
Also read $D/D1_citations.md, D2_arity.md, D3_grammar.md, D4_nohumans.md. Your role: SENIOR NATURE EDITOR + HOSTILE REFEREE. Rank every direction now on the table (memo directions 1-3 plus all new candidates from D2-D4) by expected value for Neo: P(top venue) x impact, plus P(solid specialist paper) as the floor, under a 10-week, one-person, <=\$5k budget, preferably no new human data. Drop anything resting on a citation D1 flagged as fabricated or misdescribed. For the top 3 write the referee report and the fix. At most 1,500 words." &
cx E2_feasibility "$COMMON
Also read $D/D1_citations.md, D2_arity.md, D3_grammar.md, D4_nohumans.md. Your role: FEASIBILITY ENGINEER. For the 5 most promising directions across D2-D4 and the memo, write the concrete week-by-week plan with our actual assets (Qwen3.5 0.8B/4B on Modal, Newton/cubic code in research/polybench.py and research/lm.py, the Nerode metric code, the Sketchpad pipeline), datasets to download (name, size, licence), compute cost estimates from Modal list prices, and the first 48-hour experiment that would most change our belief. At most 1,500 words." &
wait
echo "F start $(date)" >> "$D/logs/progress2.txt"
cx F_memo2 "$COMMON
Also read every file in $D (A1-A5, B1-B3, D1-D4, E1-E2). Write MEMO v2 for Neo, replacing the first-pass memo: (1) the 3 best directions ranked by expected value under one person, 10 weeks, <=\$5k, each with a draft title, a 120-word hoped-for abstract, the decisive experiment and kill, the first 48-hour experiment, verified prior art with the most dangerous paper, cost, odds for Nature / Nature Human Behaviour / a strong specialist venue, and what Neo would learn even if it fails; (2) what changed from the first memo and why; (3) rejected directions, one line each; (4) citations that turned out wrong; (5) the decisions Neo must make. Use only citations D1 verified or that you verify yourself now. Plain words; define each term on first use. At most 2,000 words."
echo "done $(date)" >> "$D/logs/progress2.txt"
